{{!
    @template theme_nit/navbar_gear_menu

    The navbar's gear button and the dropdown it opens: core's navigation rows,
    the relocated edit-mode switch, then the academy's management group.
    Rendered by theme_nit\output\core_renderer::navbar_gear_menu(), which
    returns nothing at all when every one of the three pieces is empty — so a
    guest, or a student with nothing to open, has no gear on the bar.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * nav - HTML of the core navigation rows, or ''
    * editswitch - HTML of core's edit-mode switch, or ''
    * management - HTML of the management group, or ''

    Example context (json):
    {
        "nav": "<h6 class=\"dropdown-header\">Navigation</h6><a class=\"dropdown-item\" href=\"#\">My courses</a>",
        "editswitch": "",
        "management": ""
    }
}}
<div class="dropdown nit-navmenu d-flex align-items-center">
    <a href="#" role="button" id="nit-navmenu-toggle" class="btn nit-navbar-icon" data-bs-toggle="dropdown" aria-haspopup="true" aria-expanded="false" aria-label="{{#str}}navigation, core{{/str}}">
        <i class="icon fa fa-gear fa-fw" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span class="visually-hidden">{{#str}}navigation, core{{/str}}</span>
    </a>
    <div class="dropdown-menu dropdown-menu-end nit-navbar-dropdown" aria-labelledby="nit-navmenu-toggle">
        {{! Core's navigation only — My courses / Site administration — with its
            own "Navigation" heading, so the heading is not there over nothing. }}
        {{{ nav }}}

        {{! Edit-mode toggle (moved from the bar). The wrapper is `:empty` when
            core returns no switch — CSS then hides it, so no stray row. }}
        <div class="nit-navmenu-editswitch">{{{ editswitch }}}</div>

        {{! The management screens an administrator opens daily. Empty
            (heading included) for a user without the capabilities. }}
        {{{ management }}}
    </div>
</div>
